# Network panel: the DNS provider's heading says it covers cellular too.
# Omarchy's DNS setting is one choice for the whole system, but its pills sit
# on the Wi-Fi card under "DNS PROVIDER", and on a phone that reads as Wi-Fi's
# own setting: with Wi-Fi off there was nothing to say that cellular follows
# the same choice, or where to change it. The heading names both; the
# cellular card (omamobile-shell) points back here.
#
# Against Omarchy 4.5.0-3.

diff --git i/shell/plugins/panels/network/Panel.qml w/shell/plugins/panels/network/Panel.qml
--- i/shell/plugins/panels/network/Panel.qml
+++ w/shell/plugins/panels/network/Panel.qml
@@ -1579,7 +1579,9 @@
         spacing: Style.space(10)
 
         PanelSectionHeader {
-          text: Commons.I18n.t("network.dnsProvider")
+          // One choice for every connection, cellular included: say so,
+          // since the pills sit on the Wi-Fi card.
+          text: Commons.I18n.t("network.dnsProvider") + " · WI-FI AND CELLULAR"
           foreground: root.bar.foreground
           fontFamily: root.bar.fontFamily
         }
